{"name":"Night Rider","hex":"#332e2e","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"night rider","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of nightrider."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/night_rider"}],"entries":[{"title":"Night Rider (novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Night Rider is the debut novel by American author Robert Penn Warren. It was published in the United States in 1939."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0d/NightRider.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Rider_(novel)"},{"title":"Night Rider (Elvis Presley song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Night Rider\" is a song written by Doc Pomus and Mort Shuman and originally recorded by Elvis Presley for his album Pot Luck with Elvis."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night_Rider_(Elvis_Presley_song)"},{"title":"Night","blocks":[{"text":"Night, or nighttime, is the period of darkness when the Sun is below the horizon. Daylight illuminates one side of Earth, leaving the other in darkness. The opposite of nighttime is daytime. Earth's rotation causes the appearance of sunrise and sunset. Moonlight, airglow, starlight, and light pollution dimly illuminate night. The duration of day, night, and twilight varies depending on the time of year and the observer's latitude."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg/330px-Savault_Chapel_Under_Milky_Way_BLS.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Night"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/0d/NightRider.jpg/250px-NightRider.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0d/NightRider.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://